-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1069, NORM-LOG-SPEC N19 (ruled 2026-10-26): two sides of a
-- RAND record one cell with different values while they take one event, and
-- nothing inside the RAND reads it. Nothing in the trace orders the two
-- records, so the run stops, naming the cell and both sides, whichever side
-- is written first. Equal values would not be an error.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF P
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF go

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`one` MEANS
    PARTY P
    MAY go
    WITHIN 100
    HENCE COMMIT `x` IS 1 HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`two` MEANS
    PARTY P
    MAY go
    WITHIN 100
    HENCE COMMIT `x` IS 2 HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `one` RAND `two` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY P DOES go AT 10
